1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,283
For anomaly detection, thresholds are fixed only from normal data.

2
00:00:04,283 --> 00:00:08,131
On one hour of normal operation there are zero false alarms.

3
00:00:08,131 --> 00:00:13,810
A fifty percent resistance step is detected in sixty-three seconds by the residual regression.

4
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:22,912
A cooling failure under load is detected in three hundred fifty-two seconds, compared with one thousand one hundred fifty-eight seconds for a fixed temperature threshold.

5
00:00:22,912 --> 00:00:28,009
A half-volt voltage-sensor step is caught in one second by the acute residual check.

6
00:00:28,009 --> 00:00:32,766
For robustness, we add five percent packet loss and double the sensor noise.

7
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:39,174
State-of-charge RMSE grows from zero point zero nine seven to zero point one zero eight percent.

8
00:00:39,174 --> 00:00:45,230
Voltage residual RMS doubles, as expected, and temperature accuracy is unchanged.

9
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:48,580
This is not perfection, but it is measured degradation.

